used; if you "throw" rocks while wielding a bow, you are
throwing a missile without wielding a matching launcher (adding
a -4 to your chance to hit).  (Logically, I would have thought
that the penalty for not using a matching launcher should be
higher for arrow, etc., than for rocks.  But unless the spoiler
is missing something, that's not the case.)  "Throw" arrows with
a bow, or rocks with a sling, and you add in the enchantment of
the launcher.

> Otherwise you just become skilled in arrows, etc.

Again, if I understand correctly, there's no such thing as
becoming skilled in arrows; you becomse skilled in bow.  Ditto
rocks and a sling.

It's not clear from the spoiler whether hitting something with a
rock, while wielding a bow, advances your skill in bow or not.
I would expect not (since you don't actually use the bow in such
cases), but I'd have to source dive to be sure (and I don't have
